cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mlmr, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "mlmr: A Guided Interface for Mixed-Effects and Multilevel Models"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
authors:
  - family-names: "Harris"
    given-names: "Marcus"
    affiliation: "University of Connecticut"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MarcusHarrisUConn/mlmr"
url: "https://marcusharrisphd.com/mlmr/"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "R"
  - "Shiny"
  - "multilevel modeling"
  - "mixed-effects models"
  - "hierarchical linear models"
  - "reproducible research"
abstract: >-
  mlmr is an open-source R package and Shiny application for specifying,
  fitting, understanding, and reporting mixed-effects and multilevel models. It
  provides a guided HLM-style graphical workflow while preserving transparent
  lme4 and lmerTest syntax, level-by-level and combined equations, labeled Tau
  matrices, diagnostics, APA-style tables, Nakagawa R-squared, random-intercept
  reliability, and reproducible publication bundles.
